[0.093, "o", "e"]
[0.090, "o", "r"]
[0.090, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "                                      RECENT RENOVATIONS\r\n           (as compiled by Ralph Witt Jr. for the benefit of visiting adventurers)\r\n \r\n The well house surroundings have been cleared out, allowing a reasonably unrestricted movement in\r\n all directions. Adventurers are however advised against getting lost in the dark forest, lest they\r\n be eaten by a grue.\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " Visitors from the original Adventure, should explore around the Antechamber, the Reservoir, the\r\n South Side Chamber, the Breathtaking View, the Giant Room, the Hall of the Mountain King and the\r\n Arched Hall.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n Visitors familiar with Adventure 550 will find changes in the South Side Chamber, the Anteroom,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " the Reservoir, the Lava Tube, the Rocky Beach (the one with the dinghy), and the Catacombs. And do\r\n visit the Toolroom!\r\n \r\n Visitors wise in the ways of Adventure 660 should contemplate a change at the tower entrance,\r\n explore around the Chapel and around the Rocky Beach, escape from the Giant's dungeon, use the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " chalice, get down from the Basalt Shelf, get to the island visible from the cliff's edge, and deal\r\n with the card playing dwarves. A visit to the picnicking giant may also be of benefit. Also,\r\n please note that the Spirit of the Catacombs appears to have developed a rather skewed sense of\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " humour of late - we apologise for any inconvenience.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
